  "deliberate_deviations": [
    "Retrained from scratch on OUR data: 6,983-gene frozen axis, our 611-perturbation cohort, our 5 splits. Does NOT reproduce PerturbDiff's published 0.40306 (2,000 genes / 380 perturbations / 4 cell lines).",
    "Export-level fixes vs our first port, all making it MORE faithful, none touching training: B1 checkpoint resolved from the run's own .best_ckpt_path marker (save_last=True had made the glob ambiguous, and 'last.ckpt' would have reported weights that were never selected); B2 pl.seed_everything(seed + 1000*split) before sampling, because with eta=0.0 the DDIM prediction is a deterministic function of one previously-UNSEEDED randn; M1 per-cell cov_batch taken from the PERTURBED cell's batch (upstream's get_covarates runs on the perturbed row), replacing a single constant covariate broadcast over the whole panel; M2 batch_size=len(split) so no chunk boundary can split a perturbation's cell set in two.",
    "genept arm only. The onehot twin is a separate embedding choice and is not this arm's number."
  ],
